WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:01.483
Oh, hello.

00:00:01.483 --> 00:00:02.316
I'm Gavin.

00:00:02.316 --> 00:00:03.440
This lovely slow-mo video.

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:05.220
We're going to be recreating the effects

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:08.110
of a depth charge against a submarine

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:11.020
and obviously filming
it at insane frame rates

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:13.250
not a real submarine,
they're quite expensive.

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:15.080
So we're going to use
a scale model that fits

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:17.010
inside this here fish tank.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:19.260
This video is sponsored by GoPro

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:21.870
for all the slow-mo footage
shot from outside the tank.

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:23.670
We'll be using Phantoms as normal

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:26.930
but to get shots from inside
the tank in the danger zone

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:29.360
we'll be using the GoPro Hero 9 black

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:30.780
because it's very rugged and you

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:32.470
can get a waterproof housing for it.

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:34.810
We actually had a GoPro Hero 1

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:36.801
rolling during our very
first shoot and have

00:00:36.801 --> 00:00:40.090
used them countless times
over the last 10 years.

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:41.750
And we've put them in some

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:44.920
pretty dangerous
situations, such as crash.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:46.983
Bang.

00:00:46.983 --> 00:00:47.816
Hot.

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:50.280
Wet.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:51.583
And up.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:54.610
So, I'm very thankful that

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:55.770
they're sponsoring this video today.

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:57.490
Why don't we fill the tank and get going?

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.240
Okay, here we have the sub

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:01.450
in the tank for the first experiment.

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:03.710
I'm going to be placing
a depth charge just

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:05.290
in proximity to the sub see if

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:07.820
it does any damage with
just the shockwave.

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:10.280
There's an air bladder
inside that might be ruptured

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:12.220
and it's also keeping it buoyant.

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:15.880
We will be rolling at 200
frames a second on this GoPro.

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:19.360
And I preset all the
settings with my phone.

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:22.170
However, WiFi doesn't work through water.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.610
So, once we submerge.

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:27.449
I'll have to frame it
using the screens built in.

00:01:27.449 --> 00:01:29.660
Thankfully there's one
on the front and the back

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:31.900
so I can get the correct
framing that actually

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:36.279
looks pretty epic there
looking straight down the sub.

00:01:36.279 --> 00:01:39.530
So if we put the depth charge
in front of it on this side

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:42.733
we should be able to see if
it wobbles the sub in place.

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:45.580
On the outside of the tank I'm going

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:49.200
to be filming this at
28,500 frames a second

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.500
on a Phantom, which means I'm about

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:54.330
to turn on some very bright lights.

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:57.370
Okay, we're now cooking
under the hot lights.

00:01:57.370 --> 00:02:00.120
GoPro is running at 200 in the tank.

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:03.160
The Phantom Flex4K is
running at a thousand and

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:06.760
for the nice tight explosion
shot, we're running at 28,500

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:09.510
which should be fast enough,
but we may go faster.

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:12.010
The depth charges hanging just in front

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:15.040
in the middle of the sub,
and we're ready to pop it.

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:17.743
Three, two, one, bang!

00:02:20.502 --> 00:02:22.413
Nice little puff.

00:02:26.024 --> 00:02:29.290
Whoa, you can just see the
shockwave bouncing around

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:31.340
off that glass just vibrating everything.

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:34.910
It actually moves insanely fast.

00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:37.870
If I just put an arrow
that marks the travel

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:40.090
of the shockwave as it dislodges bubbles

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:41.400
you can see how quickly it moves.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:44.145
Even dislodging bubbles from the

00:02:44.145 --> 00:02:47.993
GoPro housing itself at
28,500 frames a second.

00:02:47.993 --> 00:02:52.010
This is now over a thousand
times slower than real time,

00:02:52.010 --> 00:02:54.910
whoa, just love that expansion of gas.

00:02:54.910 --> 00:02:59.650
Just carving out an empty sphere
in the middle of the water.

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:02.810
You can see that the way
the charge separated.

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:05.430
We actually lost a lot of energy there

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:08.080
because the bottom sort of shot off

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:09.440
the pressure of the surrounding wall.

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:12.150
Now close that back up, which means

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:13.900
that not only is there
a shockwave traveling

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:16.500
around that tank from
the original explosion.

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:19.260
The moment it all slams
closed it will release

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:21.920
another shockwave which
will bounce around in there.

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:26.400
Just vibrating every single
joint of this submarine

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:29.150
it even popped open the
little escape patch.

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:30.140
Love it.

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:32.330
Okay, so now we're going to
more tightly wrap that charge

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:34.620
and hopefully give us a bit more punch

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:36.850
by wasting less energy downwards.

00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:38.040
For those curious as to why

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:39.720
I'm blasting this with so much light you

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:42.210
may remember from the
original underwater video

00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:45.840
in order to get any detail
in the explosion itself.

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:47.770
I had to stop the lens down so much

00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:51.000
that everything else
was almost pitch black.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.073
And I wanted to capture detail

00:03:53.073 --> 00:03:55.640
inside the explosion as well
as the submarine itself.

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:58.720
So by hitting it with much more
light, I can stop the lenses

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:01.590
down so that the explosions
aren't just pure white

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:04.010
and the submarine isn't pure darkness.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:07.780
I'm now slightly closer
on both cameras just to

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:10.823
really see the, the meat of the explosion.

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:15.323
Sensor it up there.

00:04:16.790 --> 00:04:18.423
Okay, here we go.

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:24.360
Three, two, one, bang!

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:25.193
Woo.

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:32.950
Blew the top off, but the
air bladder still intact.

00:04:33.105 --> 00:04:34.593
Very interesting one.

00:04:38.938 --> 00:04:41.133
Oh, I saw some great frames in there.

00:04:41.133 --> 00:04:43.220
I think I saw the thumbnail.

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:44.053
Let me find it.

00:04:44.053 --> 00:04:45.390
Let me see the thumbnail frame.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:51.240
Yeah, I think that's the one.

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:52.777
I think that's the thumbnail.

00:04:55.621 --> 00:04:58.210
Ooh, yeah just through the entire look

00:04:58.210 --> 00:05:00.270
of those vortices it's because it's threw

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:02.963
the entire explosion
forwards into the glass.

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:07.860
It's always just so interesting to

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:10.930
see explosions at such a leisurely pace.

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:12.500
You can see it's thrown
in the front of that

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:15.670
out of focus just because
it came so far forwards

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:19.402
and here you can see
the granules, the powder

00:05:19.402 --> 00:05:23.500
from the new explosion, actually
moving with such velocity.

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:27.970
They've escaped the
original explosion sphere

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:29.530
and now they're being sucked back in as it

00:05:29.530 --> 00:05:31.840
all implodes and shoots forwards.

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:34.461
Just an absolutely devastating effect on

00:05:34.461 --> 00:05:36.133
all the joints of the sub.

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:39.710
We're only about a foot underwater here

00:05:39.710 --> 00:05:41.200
but the camera is actually waterproof

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:44.560
out of the box to thirty three feet.

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:46.420
That depth charge looked great.

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:50.100
However, I really want to
bust the air bladder inside.

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:52.670
So we're going to do now same depth charge

00:05:52.670 --> 00:05:54.405
in the same place.

00:05:54.405 --> 00:05:55.810
However, there are now three charges

00:05:55.810 --> 00:05:57.480
on the top to hopefully blow the top

00:05:57.480 --> 00:05:59.130
of the sub open and there's one

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:02.440
on the inside so that the
bag definitely breaks.

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:04.740
So we should see a nice bubble

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:06.400
of air and maybe it will sink.

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:09.150
I now have a second GoPro
mounted on the bottom.

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:11.400
This one is recording in 4K

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:14.130
not slow-mo just to get the sub sinking.

00:06:14.130 --> 00:06:15.360
If it does sink.

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:18.643
This one still rolling in
slow-mo 200 frames a second

00:06:18.643 --> 00:06:23.456
is now mounted to the sub itself
and mounted extremely close

00:06:23.456 --> 00:06:26.810
to the charges. Should
get some lovely footage

00:06:26.810 --> 00:06:29.070
but we'll probably go flying, thankfully

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:31.030
because it's such a rugged camera.

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:34.040
The footage will be saved in theory

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:36.550
Three, two, one. Bang!

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:37.593
Whoa!

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:43.280
Can't wait to see the footage on that.

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:44.583
Where's the GoPro landed?

00:06:45.910 --> 00:06:47.020
Oh yeah, it did.

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:50.240
Okay. It flew off, but let me see

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:52.370
if I can see if it's rolling.

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:55.483
I still see a flashing red
light and that's very good news.

00:06:58.180 --> 00:07:01.290
Whoa, those charges on top of meaty

00:07:01.290 --> 00:07:03.920
just sent a shockwave
all the way down the end

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:07.239
snapping the sub and it's rear joint.

00:07:07.239 --> 00:07:10.217
And the fact that you can
see the surface of the water

00:07:10.217 --> 00:07:12.120
it really shows you how much that glass

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:13.520
is wobbling back and forth.

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:16.720
Whoa. So the, the big shot is on top

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:19.040
went off before the depth charge on side.

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:23.310
And you can see tiny cavitation
bubbles working their way

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:25.560
from right to left as it travels

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:28.760
just tearing up that plastic of the sub.

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:31.710
Speed it up and back and forth
that you can see its travel.

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:38.930
It also shot a lovely bubble ring

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:40.407
from that hole directly below the charge.

00:07:40.407 --> 00:07:44.040
So the air bladder
inside definitely popped

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:46.170
but the shockwaves are
just bouncing the air

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:48.300
around inside and the
depth charge there it

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:51.240
must've been waterlogged because

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:54.040
pretty much just coughed instead

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:57.510
of its usual explosion,
GoPro still on there.

00:07:57.510 --> 00:07:58.670
Oh, there it goes.

00:07:58.670 --> 00:08:00.480
Yeah. The air took a long time to come

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:03.934
out just because the shockwaves
were bouncing it around

00:08:03.934 --> 00:08:06.002
inside sending some of it down.

00:08:06.002 --> 00:08:08.533
Some of it left and right, mental.

00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:12.450
Now let's see if the GoPro saw anything

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:14.123
useful before it was chucked.

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:16.283
Oh yeah, oh yeah.

00:08:16.283 --> 00:08:18.230
We saw some good frames there.

00:08:18.230 --> 00:08:19.560
No issues with the footage.

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:22.610
A lot of times that I've put
cameras near massive shockwaves

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:24.950
like that you will get
artifacts and glitches

00:08:24.950 --> 00:08:27.963
but I didn't see an issue with
any of those frames there.

00:08:29.410 --> 00:08:32.411
Whoa, that's the other one landing

00:08:32.411 --> 00:08:34.720
that shockwave was so powerful.

00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:38.470
It actually jumped the
very heavy metal bar

00:08:38.470 --> 00:08:41.523
keeping the sub way down.

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:45.367
Well there, we have it,
some lovely looking footage

00:08:45.367 --> 00:08:48.170
and as expected, the
GoPro's got chucked all

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:50.520
over the place especially
the ones I mounted to

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:52.498
the submarine itself,
but they all survived.

00:08:52.498 --> 00:08:54.572
Got the footage off all of them and

00:08:54.572 --> 00:08:57.270
did a damn good job in my opinion.

00:08:57.270 --> 00:08:59.880
If you care about my
opinion on this camera

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:01.640
the things I like about it over

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:04.810
the previous versions is mainly this clip.

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:07.580
I'm not sure when this
started my previous GoPro

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:09.770
you need an external housing
to mount it and stuff.

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:12.010
I love that it's built
into the camera body now.

00:09:12.010 --> 00:09:14.530
And the front screen is
great when you can't get

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:15.960
around the back of the camera.

00:09:15.960 --> 00:09:18.290
If you want a Hero 9 black of your own

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:21.450
go to gopro.com/slowmoguys

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:23.900
Big old thanks to GoPro
for sponsoring this video.

00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:26.080
Even bigger thanks to you for watching it.

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:27.670
If you like Slow Mo in general

